    "snippet": "May 25, 2022         The inotify mechanism (and its predecessor, dnotify) were added to the kernel to support the Samba server, he said. Remote systems that are talking to a Samba server on Linux can see those kinds of changes, but remote Linux clients cannot. The client API changed at some point so that network filesystems have no easy way to register to receive these kinds of events. For SMB, he added an ioctl() command that can be used wait on notifications of these changes.   Summarize",
