    "title": "linux - How to execute a command whenever a file changes? - Super User",
    "snippet": "Aug 28, 2010         Polling is the only portable way, but most systems have a file change notification mechanism (inotify on Linux, kqueue on FreeBSD, ...). You have a severe quoting problem when you do $cmd, but fortunately that's easily fixable: ditch the cmd variable and execute \"$@\". File changes happening during the do ...; will be missed. Slow when using in recursive mode. Therefor I made a helper script that uses inotifywait without those limitations: inotifyexec.   Summarize",
